  - Father
  - Father
  - Little Girl
  - Little Girl
  - Little Girl
  - Little Girl
  - Little Girl
  - Father
  - Father
  - Little Girl
  dialogue:
  - Good morning, Father.
  - What happened last night?
  - Last night? Nothing happened last night.
  - But I heard your shotgun.
  - And when I went to check, a monster chased me.
  - Oh, yes. I shot the monster last night, that's what you heard.
  - 'But you just said- I saw the monster after I heard the shot. '
  - No it was before. You were probably tired and scared.
  - It's not surprising you misremembered.
  - '*Thinking* Father is of no help, but maybe his journals are.'
  - '*Thinking* He journals every day, maybe he wrote something about last night. '
  - '*Thinking* He keeps his study locked when he''s not there.'
  - '*Thinking* I need the key he keeps on his nightstand at night.'
  - Where is the master bedroom key?
  - It's by Grandma in the living room.
  - But I don't want you going into my bedroom, so don't take it!
  - Of course not, Father.
  portrait:
  - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7974f0af01e77c2459ba5035c58aff24, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7974f0af01e77c2459ba5035c58aff24, type: 3}
